<TeXmacs|2.1.4>

<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Structured text>

  <TeXmacs> is a <em|structured> editor: besides the text itself, a
  <TeXmacs> document records what the different parts of the text <em|are>.
  A section title is not just a line in a large bold font, it is marked as
  a section title; an emphasized word is marked as emphasized; a theorem is
  marked as a theorem. The <em|style> of the document then decides how each
  kind of text is displayed. This chapter shows how to work with this
  structure.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|Emphasizing text|tut-emphasize.en.tm>

    <branch|Sections|tut-sections.en.tm>

    <branch|The cursor and the structure|tut-cursor.en.tm>

    <branch|Theorems, proofs and lists|tut-environments.en.tm>
